sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch11-19> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch11-19--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch11-19--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on wolfram2002-ch11-19: resolvable-now, resolvability 0.74" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.745"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "resolvable-now" ;
    dct:type "resolution-route/proof" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.7"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "If the class is defined by ultimately uniform or repetitive behavior for every input, non-universality is a theorem: only finitely much information about the input survives, or the surviving information is periodic. That argument can be checked on the elementary examples by computing periods and dependence cones. The book's phrase about limited distance is slightly too narrow for shifting class-2 rules, but those rules still fail universality for the same periodicity reason." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Formalize class 1 and class 2 as evolution that, for every initial condition, becomes uniform or periodic with a bound depending only on the rule. Prove that such a system has a finite effective memory and cannot emulate a Turing machine. A universality construction inside that class would refute the claim." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Some rules usually called class 2 carry signals arbitrarily far, so non-universality then rests on the form of the reachable configurations rather than on a strict distance bound." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/wolfram2002-ch11-19--grok--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/wolfram2002-ch11-19--grok--dataset-2> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch11-19--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of wolfram2002-ch11-19 by Grok 4.7: 0.7" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.7"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch11-19--grok> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch11-19> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/wolfram2002-ch11-19--grok--operationalizability> .
